WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.979
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEFL preparation.

2
00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:08.770
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:16.528
Unit ten: Listening: Note-taking and Inference. Today you will take efficient notes and infer meaning from tone and attitude.

4
00:00:16.828 --> 00:00:19.399
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:23.520
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.383 --> 00:00:25.605
Abbreviation.

7
00:00:26.617 --> 00:00:29.324
Abbreviation means a short form of a word.

8
00:00:29.917 --> 00:00:32.067
Use an abbreviation like govt.

9
00:00:32.683 --> 00:00:35.556
Your turn. Say: Abbreviation.

10
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.657
Abbreviation.

11
00:00:40.417 --> 00:00:41.162
Symbol.

12
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:44.649
Symbol means a sign that stands for a word.

13
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.029
Use an arrow as a symbol.

14
00:00:47.617 --> 00:00:50.432
Your turn. Say: Symbol.

15
00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.163
Symbol.

16
00:00:54.917 --> 00:00:55.895
Outline.

17
00:00:56.883 --> 00:00:59.661
Outline means a simple plan of main points.

18
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.901
Make an outline of the talk.

19
00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:05.030
Your turn. Say: Outline.

20
00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:08.891
Outline.

21
00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:10.581
Attitude.

22
00:01:11.583 --> 00:01:13.954
Attitude means how a speaker feels.

23
00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:16.933
The speaker's attitude is positive.

24
00:01:17.517 --> 00:01:20.297
Your turn. Say: Attitude.

25
00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:24.169
Attitude.

26
00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:26.208
Sarcasm.

27
00:01:27.217 --> 00:01:30.749
Sarcasm means saying the opposite to be funny or critical.

28
00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.152
She spoke with sarcasm.

29
00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:36.414
Your turn. Say: Sarcasm.

30
00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:40.407
Sarcasm.

31
00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:42.151
Hesitate.

32
00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:45.498
Hesitate means to pause because of doubt.

33
00:01:46.083 --> 00:01:48.036
He hesitated before answering.

34
00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:51.291
Your turn. Say: Hesitate.

35
00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:55.007
Hesitate.

36
00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:56.890
Emphasis.

37
00:01:57.883 --> 00:02:00.672
Emphasis means extra stress on a word.

38
00:02:01.283 --> 00:02:03.364
The speaker puts emphasis on 'never'.

39
00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:06.602
Your turn. Say: Emphasis.

40
00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:10.642
Emphasis.

41
00:02:11.383 --> 00:02:12.373
Implied.

42
00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:15.882
Implied means suggested but not stated.

43
00:02:16.483 --> 00:02:18.529
The implied meaning is a criticism.

44
00:02:19.117 --> 00:02:21.618
Your turn. Say: Implied.

45
00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:25.479
Implied.

46
00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:29.987
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.337
Visal, how can I take notes faster?

48
00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:47.403
Use abbreviations and symbols. For example, write govt for government and an arrow for causes. Notes should be short enough to read in a few seconds.

49
00:02:48.517 --> 00:02:49.924
Why does tone matter?

50
00:02:51.017 --> 00:03:02.678
Some questions ask about the speaker's attitude or what the speaker really means. A pause, a rising voice or an emphasised word can show doubt, surprise or sarcasm.

51
00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.794
What should I do with an inference question?

52
00:03:06.883 --> 00:03:17.419
Combine your notes with the tone you heard. Choose the option that matches both the words and the feeling, and avoid answers that need extra information.

53
00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:20.067
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:20.917 --> 00:03:25.087
Grammar focus: Strategy: short notes, careful tone.

55
00:03:25.387 --> 00:03:26.609
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:27.317 --> 00:03:31.046
I write 'govt → tax' for the government causes a tax change.

57
00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:35.169
She hesitated, so she probably doubts the idea.

58
00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:41.630
Use abbreviations and symbols in notes. For inference, combine what is said with how it is said.

59
00:03:42.383 --> 00:03:45.755
Be careful! Don't say: I ignore the speaker's tone.

60
00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.396
Say: I listen to the tone as well.

61
00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:51.976
Tone shows meaning.

62
00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:55.338
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:57.773
Understanding Attitude.

64
00:03:58.073 --> 00:04:01.466
A professor says, Well, that plan is certainly ambitious.

65
00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:04.722
She pauses before the word ambitious.

66
00:04:05.733 --> 00:04:08.418
The class understands that she may doubt the plan.

67
00:04:09.433 --> 00:04:12.698
A student writes govt, plan, doubt in her notes.

68
00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:16.582
She chooses the answer that matches the professor's tone.

69
00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:21.866
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:22.717 --> 00:04:24.809
Abbreviations make notes blank.

71
00:04:25.109 --> 00:04:28.716
A, harder to read. B, faster. C, longer.

72
00:04:32.267 --> 00:04:34.127
The answer is B: faster.

73
00:04:35.283 --> 00:04:37.620
A pause before a word can show blank.

74
00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:41.283
A, a date. B, a place. C, doubt.

75
00:04:44.833 --> 00:04:46.926
The answer is C: doubt.

76
00:04:48.083 --> 00:04:49.955
An implied meaning is blank.

77
00:04:50.255 --> 00:04:55.406
A, suggested, not stated. B, spelled out. C, a number.

78
00:04:58.967 --> 00:05:01.907
The answer is A: suggested, not stated.

79
00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:05.317
What does the professor think of the plan?

80
00:05:05.617 --> 00:05:09.711
A, she ignores it. B, she doubts it. C, she loves it.

81
00:05:13.267 --> 00:05:15.568
The answer is B: she doubts it.

82
00:05:16.717 --> 00:05:18.414
Which symbol means 'causes'?

83
00:05:18.714 --> 00:05:22.600
A, a circle. B, a star. C, an arrow.

84
00:05:26.133 --> 00:05:27.924
The answer is C: an arrow.

85
00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:32.297
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:35.544
How do you take notes and understand attitude?

87
00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:45.862
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:46.162 --> 00:06:01.472
I use abbreviations and symbols to write short notes. I listen for pauses and stressed words because they show how the speaker feels. For an inference question, I choose the option that matches both the words and the tone.

89
00:06:01.772 --> 00:06:03.562
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:09.842
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: short notes, careful tone.

91
00:06:10.142 --> 00:06:14.397
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

92
00:06:14.697 --> 00:06:17.233
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

93
00:06:17.533 --> 00:06:20.232
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

